            "review_title": "Review at Bia hoi Ha Noi",
            "review_text": "LIZandELT\nPerth, Australia306 contributions\n0\nDisappointing staff attitude.\nFeb 2024 • Couples\nMyself and husband and another couple ate here this evening. As we are not locals the waitress helped with the menu. My friend and I wanted something light. As I have some serious health issues I requested vegetarian spring rolls. The meal arrived and I felt it wasn’t right. Clearly they had mince in them. My reaction ( feeling unwell before finishing the short walk home) made we certain of this. I get server reaction to pork mince. I had offered one roll to my friend who stated he thought it was pork also. \n\nMy mistake to continue to eat once I suspected it was not vegetarian. But to look up to see waitress watching for my reaction was extremely disappointing. The lady had engaged nicely before delivering my meal but chose to avoid the table once I had started eating. \n\nClearly a restaurant for people who have no allergies, can read Vietnamese for themselves rather than be at the mercy of wait staff.\nRead more\nWritten February 24, 2024",
